Hey friends, this is Keith Ellison, your Minnesota Attorney General. And I'm proud that my office is defending a state law, the Minnesota Dream Act. And what it says is that if you're a person who has gone to Minnesota schools for years and you've come to this country because your parents brought you and you were too young to make a decision for yourself, that you can go to a Minnesota college and pay in-state tuition. Anybody who moves to Minnesota and makes Minnesota their home can do that. And yet the federal government is suing Minnesota because we're trying to build the most educated group of young people we can to make our state stronger. And they're suing us for that and they're falsely accusing us of discrimination if you can believe it. Bottom line, though, is that these young people are they're really grateful that the Minnesota Attorney General's office is standing for this law that is giving them opportunity. And they sent me all of these cards. And so here's here's just a few of them. I'm

